Growing up Norm never really viewed himself as creative, being stuck into logical thinking.
However it was always sort of around the edges, especially showing up in relation to
problem solving.

As an adult though, he really began to get in deep touch with his creative side. Just as a
hobby he has explored and experiemented with chainmail making (fashion and jewelry), makeup
application, fashion design, alchohol ink abstracts, and a bit of blacksmithing. Much more
seriously, he has spent half a decade working on writing, with 3 novels making some serious
progress and numerous other projects with words. He has also spent over twenty-five years
working to catch light onto film or sensors and progress that to some real visuals (the
imagery on this site doesn't even begin to show his range).

As a coach he can help you learn to open up, to listen to yourself and help you to uncover
what you really want to be chasing as an aesthetic. How do you create the art that you want to
and how do you balance that against the need to actually pay for the tools and materials
you need to produce your art or to live.

What do you really want to say, produce, and do with your creativity, and in what aspects of
your life?




